Rationale: These states are located along the edges of the grid and have three adjacent connections (two directions and one "wall" or obstacle). The agent can move in two possible directions from these states to progress towards the goal.

**Abstract State 3: Obstacle-Adjacent States**
Clustered states: {2, 5, 8, 11, 14, 17, 20, 23, 26, 29, 32, 35, 38, 41, 44}
Rationale: These states are adjacent to obstacles (X) and have limited connectivity. The agent can move in only one or two possible directions from these states to progress towards the goal.

**Abstract State 4: Interior States**
Clustered states: {9, 12, 15, 18, 21, 24, 27, 30, 33, 36, 39, 42, 45, 47, 50, 51, 52, 53, 54, 56, 57, 58, 59, 60, 61, 62, 63}
